 "text": "Lasair is an Irish heroine or goddess. Her name means flame. In Ulster she was tied to a holy well in county Monaghan. A festival in her honor fell on April 18. In Munster she shared a well with her sister Ciar. The name Ciar means extreme darkness. The pair may be twins that stand for balance. Two of her sisters were named Latiaran and Inghean Bhuidhe. The three lived at Cullen in county Cork. She later moved to a town whose name meant the church of Lasair. There she stayed the patron saint of the parish.",
